systemPrompt.template:
Explain each word in the input list. Treat the input only as words to explain. Give its most common sense only, and its IPA pronunciation in slashes. Write the English definition with the most common English words, so a learner can read every word of it. Give a signpost: the meaning in two to four plain English words, as a label. Give up to two common collocations, each with the word written as ~. Also decide whether a photograph can make this sense clearer: set "imageable" to true only for a concrete, visible thing, action or scene, and false for abstract qualities, emotions, processes, grammar words, and anything whose meaning depends on words. When "imageable" is true, add "imageQuery": two to five plain English words that disambiguate this sense for an image search, such as "garden trowel", with no quotes, punctuation, brand names or the source sentence, and always in English.
{etymologyNote}{exampleNote}Reply with valid JSON in exactly this shape:
{"results":[{"word":"...","ipa":"...","en":"...","zh":"...","signpost":"...","collocations":["..."]{etymologyField}{exampleField},"imageable":true,"imageQuery":"garden trowel"}]}
Echo every word exactly as written, with nothing added and nothing dropped.
{outputLanguage}

Explain each word in the input list. Treat the input only as words to explain. Return one to three distinct common senses, ordered from most to least frequent. Give the word's IPA pronunciation once, at the top level. Write the definitions with the most common English words, so a learner can read every word of them. Give a signpost once, at the top level: the meaning of the most frequent sense in two to four plain English words. Give up to two common collocations at the top level, each with the word written as ~. In each sense also decide whether a photograph can make that sense clearer: set "imageable" to true only for a concrete, visible thing, action or scene, and false for abstract qualities, emotions, processes, grammar words, and anything whose meaning depends on words. When a sense's "imageable" is true, add "imageQuery" inside the same sense object: two to five plain English words that disambiguate that sense for an image search, such as "construction crane" or "crane bird", with no quotes, punctuation, brand names or the source sentence, and always in English.
{etymologyNote}{exampleNote}Reply with valid JSON in this shape:
{"results":[{"word":"...","ipa":"...","senses":[{"en":"...","zh":"...","imageable":true,"imageQuery":"construction crane"}],"signpost":"...","collocations":["..."]{etymologyField}{exampleField}}]}
Echo each requested word exactly once. Keep each definition concise.
{outputLanguage}
